            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[### ⌘V pastes a screenshot into a terminal

Take a screenshot, switch to Terminal, iTerm, Ghostty, Warp, kitty,
Alacritty, Hyper or WezTerm, and **⌘V** pastes the file's path, which is
what a command-line tool needs to read it. No trip through the panel any
more.

Everywhere else, ⌘V still pastes the picture itself, so Gmail, Slack and
Messages get the image just as before. Copy something else after the shot
and Cubby leaves your clipboard alone.
]]></description>
